ge>101</fpage><lpage>7</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">18259880</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="R8"><label>8</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Shrestha</surname><given-names>PM</given-names></name><name><surname>Noll</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Liesack</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Phylogenetic identity, growth-response time and rRNA operon copy number of soil bacteria indicate different stages of community succession</article-title><source>Environ Microbiol</source><year>2007</year><volume>9</volume><fpage>2464</fpage><lpage>74</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17803772</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="R9"><label>9</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Fierer</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Schimel</surname><given-names>JP</given-names></name><name><surname>Holden</surname><given-names>PA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Variations in microbial community composition through two soil depth profiles</article-title><source>Soil Biol Biochem</source><year>2003</year><volume>35</volume><fpage>167</fpage><lpage>76</lpage></element-citation></ref><ref id="R10"><label>10</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Margesin</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Labbe</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Schinner</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Greer</surname><given-names>CW</given-names></name><name><surname>Whyte</surname><given-names>LG</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Characterization of hydrocarbon-degrading microbial populations in contaminated and pristine alpine soils</article-title><source>Appl Environ Microbiol</source><year>2003</year><volume>69</volume><fpage>3085</fpage><lpage>92</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12788702</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="R11"><label>11</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Whyte</surname><given-names>LG</given-names></name><name><surname>Schultz</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>van Beilen</surname><given-names>JB</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Prevalence of alkane monooxygenase genes in Arctic and Antarctic hydrocarbon-contaminated and pristine soils</article-title><source>FEMS Microbiol Ecol</source><year>2002</year><volume>41</volume><fpage>141</fpage><lpage>50</lpage></element-citation></ref><ref id="R12"><label>12</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>D'Annibale</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Rosetto</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Leonardi</surname><given-names>V</given-names></name><name><surname>Federici</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Petruccioli</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Pole of autochthonous filamentous fungi in bioremediation of a soil historically contaminated with aromatic hydrocarbons</article-title><source>Appl Environ Microbiol</source><year>2006</year><volume>72</volume><fpage>28</fpage><lpage>36</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16391021</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="R13"><label>13</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Zytner</surname><given-names>RG</given-names></name><name><surname>Salb</surname><given-names>AC</given-names></name><name><surname>Stiver</surname><given-names>WH</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Bioremediation of diesel fuel contaminated soil: comparison of individual compounds to complex mixtures</article-